<title>DUBAI: Oman cuts June crude selling price to $17.75.</title>
<headline>Oman cuts June crude selling price to $17.75.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oman has cut the official selling price of its crude oil lifted in June to $17.75 a barrel from $19.25 the previous month, an Omani oil official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The move follows the Abu Dhabi National Oil Company's (ADNOC) decision announced on Tuesday to cut its prices by $1.35-1.70 a barrel for June exports.</p>
<p>Non-OPEC Oman sets its selling price in line with spot market developments.</p>
<p>-- Dubai Newsroom, +971 4 6071255. SS</p>
</text>
